{"nodes": [{"id": "craft_docs_craft_risk_assessment_code_evidence_risk_register", "label": "Craft Risk Register Code Evidence", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "craft/docs/craft-risk-assessment-code-evidence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "before-baseline for risks R1-R14 with every claim tied to a file/line read directly; errata section corrects the parent assessment where it overstates (SAST/SCA tooling described as live but absent, AST validation is function discovery not a language-mode gate, Docker! SSH fallback is a hardcoded credential)"}, {"id": "craft_docs_craft_risk_assessment_code_evidence_r1_runspace_state_bleed", "label": "R1 Cross-Tenant Runspace State Bleed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "craft/docs/craft-risk-assessment-code-evidence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "exclusive worker checkout + per-invocation global-variable reset make concurrent bleed impossible; residual surface is the by-design name-keyed shared caches and module-scoped variables which cleanup deliberately skips; guardrail = tenant-keyed cache keys, owned by the platform even though the caching discipline is application-layer"}, {"id": "craft_docs_craft_risk_assessment_code_evidence_r4_client_principal_trust", "label": "R4 x-ms-client-principal Platform Trust", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "craft/docs/craft-risk-assessment-code-evidence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "accepted rather than stripped in-app: Azure App Service EasyAuth guarantees external requests cannot set principal headers, so an in-app strip duplicated the platform guarantee and was reverted; residual only if the container is exposed directly without EasyAuth, an unsupported configuration"}, {"id": "craft_docs_craft_risk_assessment_code_evidence_r8_fail_closed_storage", "label": "R8 Fail-Closed Storage Resolution", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "craft/docs/craft-risk-assessment-code-evidence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "three services silently fell back to UseDevelopmentStorage=true; replaced by single StorageSettings.ResolveConnection that throws at startup unless the dev emulator is explicitly opted in, so production misconfig fails loudly instead of pointing RBAC/state at a nonexistent emulator"}, {"id": "craft_docs_craft_risk_assessment_code_evidence_oidc_subsystem_removal", "label": "R5/R14 Native OIDC Subsystem Removal", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "craft/docs/craft-risk-assessment-code-evidence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "native OIDC login, in-memory session store, and the client-secret-derived AES session key were removed entirely; EasyAuth owns token validation and sessions, Craft only transforms the injected header and enforces allowedUsers authorization; ValidateIdToken dropped as dead code along with the IdentityModel NuGet packages"}, {"id": "craft_docs_craft_risk_assessment_code_evidence_r7_kestrel_limits", "label": "R7 Kestrel Limits and Rate Limiter", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "craft/docs/craft-risk-assessment-code-evidence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "limits now unconditional: 600s default timeout, 100 MB body cap, 200 connection cap, slow-loris data rates; per-client fixed-window rate limiter (300 req/10s) partitioned by principal name falling back to first X-Forwarded-For hop so anonymous callers behind the load balancer are not collapsed into one partition"}], "edges": [{"source": "craft_docs_craft_risk_assessment_code_evidence_risk_register", "tar